---
description: Audio-thread rules for DSP and processor code
globs: plugins/**/Source/**/*.{h,cpp},shared/dsp/**/*.h
alwaysApply: false
---

Code reachable from `processBlock` must be realtime safe:

- No allocation/deallocation (`new`, vector growth, `std::string`, `juce::String`, buffer resizing). Preallocate in `prepareToPlay`.
- No blocking locks (`std::mutex`, `CriticalSection`). Atomics or `SpinLock` try-locks only; on failure keep previous data.
- No I/O, logging, `DBG`, exceptions, or message-thread calls.
- Smooth every audible gain/parameter change (`animalaudio::dsp::OnePoleSmoother`); assume hard-edged curves.
- Use `juce::ScopedNoDenormals`; support any block size and sample rate; `getPlayHead()` may be null, always keep a free-run fallback.
- Audio -> UI via relaxed atomics; UI -> audio via immutable snapshots (see `CurveState::fetchTable`).
- Keep DSP JUCE-free where possible and cover it with Catch2 tests.
